--- !u!114 &252498381
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 252498379}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2efde7e9e75a7e747817347127bcb875, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TextTreeChooser
  PossibleSequencesMorale:
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The people of the town are in high spirits! The streets are full of friendly
        smiling faces who give you many pets and treats.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 90
    knightHealthThreshold: 0
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The people of the town are slightly nervous. The streets seem less lively
        and when people approach you with pets and treats, they also ask after the
        knight's health.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 60
    knightHealthThreshold: 0
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'The people of the town are very tense. Very few sorry looking townspeople
        are still out by the time you get back and they all walk in groups. The baker
        asks if the town should prepare for the worst. '
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 30
    knightHealthThreshold: 0
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You don't see anyone on the way into town, aside from the woodworker
        fortifying the end of the town leading into the forest who doesn't look at
        you. The buildings are boarded up and you get no treats.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 0
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  PossibleSequencesKnightHealth:
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The knight's condition is stable and even threw your ball a few times
        before you snuggled up and fell asleep.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 6
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'Despite the knight reassuring you with lots of cuddles and pets that
        you just had a bad day, your confidence is completely shattered after failing
        so badly. '
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You spend the rest of week sighing randomly and laying with your head
        and paws out.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The knight deteriorates quickly, and your week gets worse when you wake
        up to a completely silent bedroom.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'Bad ending 1: Bark Worse than Bite'
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 5
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You fall asleep on top of the knight, feeling the cool press of armour
        on your fur.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: When you next wake up, the witch is standing by the bed glaring at you.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 965250240303679006, guid: e30f6a1cffa541d448ec9b1537530ea9, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: "You didn\u2019t visit me today :( That makes me sad, bubba."
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 965250240303679006, guid: e30f6a1cffa541d448ec9b1537530ea9, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: "Why don\u2019t you make it up to me by having a sleepover tonight?"
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: "Instead of barking like you would at any other intruder, you decide
        to go with the witch. You\u2019ll be back before the knight even notices
        you\u2019re gone tomorrow! "
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: "The next day, however, the forest doesn\u2019t let you leave. No matter
        how much you whine, bark, bite or beg, the witch only pouts at you."
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 965250240303679006, guid: e30f6a1cffa541d448ec9b1537530ea9, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: "Come on, bubba! Now you get to live with the fun parent <3! You\u2019ll
        learn to love it in the forest :) "
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 965250240303679006, guid: e30f6a1cffa541d448ec9b1537530ea9, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: ...and eventually forget every worthless thing in that town.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 965250240303679006, guid: e30f6a1cffa541d448ec9b1537530ea9, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You never learn what happens to the knight or the town.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'Bad ending 2: Unofficial Custody Change'
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 4
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You tried not to lose hope.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'Surely, you would be able to find a different solution, or the knight
        would get better without help. '
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Yet, every time you came home from adventuring, the knight looked worse
        and worse.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: After the next weekend passes, you lay stubbornly on the knight.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Don't worry your little head, my good boy. I'm not dead yet.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: ...You're doing great, you know.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Hey, don't look so sad. None of this is your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b0457ef8882733244885214b1de98c91, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: I love you so much. You are precious. The town is in good hands.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Now, go on. They... I'm relying on you.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The knight is dead when you get back home.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The townspeople help with the funeral and there isn't a dry eye in attendance.
        Especially not yours.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The baker lifts you out of the casket despite your efforts to cling on
        what remains of your knight. She holds you close when the tradesmen lower
        it down and bury it.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd3e8ea5a61f2124ab5bd38d4210a117, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 3179903954906608466, guid: 7c3720bde69f77045ad01bbd2351c262, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Hey, why don't you come live with me, sweetie? It must be lonely in that
        big house. We can look after each other.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Hey, don't look so sad. None of this is your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b0457ef8882733244885214b1de98c91, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Hey, don't look so sad. None of this is your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b0457ef8882733244885214b1de98c91, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 6153638517153327099, guid: ffcf93ef33950864583a376d4cd0d5e6, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Hey, don't look so sad. None of this is your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b0457ef8882733244885214b1de98c91, type: 3}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 3
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The knight and apothecary reassured you that you can try again to pick
        enough herbs.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: When you waddle into the forest the next day though, there are no herbs
        at all.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: In fact, the herbs never grow in the forest again.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The apothecary tries to make do with what you have, but that only delays
        the inevitable.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 2266272501717668400, guid: 90da6119d6ae2034d83b0c4b7a58492f, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 2
      Line: I'm sorry, dog. There's nothing more I can do for you two.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd3e8ea5a61f2124ab5bd38d4210a117, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 2266272501717668400, guid: 90da6119d6ae2034d83b0c4b7a58492f, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 3
      Line: I... I know it's not my place to say, but I hope you know that this wasn't
        your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You know it wasn't your fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 3
      Line: But it was someone else's fault.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: The witch controls the forest; he chooses what grows.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Now, the witch will know how it feels to lose something precious.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 49296a8c99898f54cb1594373a036846, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 2266272501717668400, guid: 90da6119d6ae2034d83b0c4b7a58492f, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: I'm sorry, dog. There's nothing more I can do for you two.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 2
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  - DialogueTree:
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: You wonder if the witch was being honest or if it was a mean trick.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 2266272501717668400, guid: 90da6119d6ae2034d83b0c4b7a58492f, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: My medicine already seems to have improved your condition
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 2266272501717668400, guid: 90da6119d6ae2034d83b0c4b7a58492f, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Please still take it easy for the next couple of days. But if you pass
        a few more checkups, I will clear you to start adventuring again.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: For the first time in a week, you walk to the edge of the forest with
        the knight. You keep stopping to look at the knight like you think this is
        all too good to be true. Despite nearly tripping over you multiple times,
        the knight only laughs at your antics.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: To your further shock, you find the forest completely rid of any monsters,
        traces of magic or the witch. It seems that papa really was telling the truth...
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 3775439028298555850, guid: 74f122a1ecb0b594c95de78a006d2559, type: 3}
      TextSpeed: 0.5
      Line: You did it, buddy! The witch is gone. I am so proud of you, my goodest
        boy!
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Your tail wags as the knight spoils you with pets.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c999fc6f85824e147a0cd66eb210482f, type: 3}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: It's only a matter of time before another magical beast takes residence
        in the forest. But, for the little time it will last, the town enjoys the
        calm.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Somedays, you miss the witch. You kick your legs in your sleep, wondering
        if you could have done anything differently for a better outcome.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: Mostly though, you and the knight enjoy the time off, keeping busy with
        helping the townspeople with less important errands.
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    - Speaker: {fileID: 0}
      TextSpeed: 1
      Line: 'Neutral ending: Full Physical Custody'
      DogSoundEffect: {fileID: 0}
    townMoraleThreshold: 0
    knightHealthThreshold: 1
    currentDayThreshold: 0
  PossibleSequencesCurrentDay: []
